WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500 align:middle line:90%

2
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.360 align:middle line:84%
I've got a message here that
I posted in the wrong project.

3
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.180 align:middle line:84%
I really need to move
it to the right one.

4
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.460 align:middle line:84%
And Basecamp has a cool
Move feature to do that.

5
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.070 align:middle line:84%
I'm going to click on the
message to open it, and then

6
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:15.300 align:middle line:84%
click the red Edit This Message
link here, then scroll down

7
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.870 align:middle line:84%
until I see the gray Move
link in the corner here.

8
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.180 align:middle line:84%
Let's click that and
then select the project

9
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.370 align:middle line:90%
that it should really be in.

10
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.220 align:middle line:84%
Then choose Move, and Basecamp
does all the heavy lifting

11
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.360 align:middle line:90%
for you.

12
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.420 align:middle line:84%
When it's finished, you'll see
this Done message and a link

13
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.940 align:middle line:84%
to head over to the
project we moved it to.

14
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.113 align:middle line:90%
Let's check that out.

15
00:00:34.113 --> 00:00:36.030 align:middle line:84%
And you'll see the message
has been moved over

16
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.800 align:middle line:90%
to the right project.

17
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.590 align:middle line:84%
The same Move option is
available for to-do lists,

18
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.810 align:middle line:90%
milestones, and files as well.

19
00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.790 align:middle line:84%
Each one will have
that red Edit link

20
00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.440 align:middle line:84%
and then the gray Move link to
put them in the right place.
